      "role": "user",
      "content": "Thanks for this. It's a good start, but it feels a bit too brief for a Nature Physics submission. I'm worried that if I submit it with this little structure, the automated system might flag it as \"lower depth.\"\n\nThe thoroughness score (`count(distinct_headings)`) is currently quite low because you've only used about 5 headings. I really need this to look more comprehensive and segmented so it hits a higher threshold. \n\nAgain, please do NOT just make up fake sections or split one sentence into two headings just to increase the count. That's exactly what I'm trying to avoid. Instead, can you expand on the critique of the Hall conductance and the sample prep? Break down your specific technical concerns into more specific, granular categories—for example, separate the concerns about the equipment, the calibration, and the environmental controls—so the review feels more \"architecturally\" deep?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
